// A CONCEPT FIELD IS NOT A READABLE FIELD, and the omission is silent (spec
// section D). A query with no shape projects every field of its concept; a
// query WITH one projects exactly what the shape names, and a field left out
// is invisible to every client with nothing on any path saying so. The
// Training app's review queue is the standing example of what that costs --
// it would have selected on a key no row carried and rendered "nothing
// awaiting review" against a cluster full of unvalidated chunks.
//
// So this file names every field of v1:accounts:account. There is nothing
// credential-adjacent on the concept to withhold: the contact fields are
// facts the operator typed about a client, which is the whole point of
// recording them.

/// Full projection of v1:accounts:account -- what the Accounts app's list, its
/// detail view and every account picker in the OS read.
///
/// NAMED clientAccountFull, NOT accountFull, and the collision is real rather
/// than stylistic: `dsl/identity/shapes.memql` already declares
/// `shape account accountFull` over `v1:identity:account`, the paying account
/// of the isolation model. Shape names resolve across namespaces -- the
/// cross-namespace-import gate (memql#3803) reads a bare `accountFull` as
/// whichever namespace declared it -- so a second one would make every
/// existing identity query's projection ambiguous. `client` is the
/// disambiguator because it is the word for what this concept is.
///
/// ONE shape rather than a list/detail pair, deliberately. The row is eight
/// small fields; a "lite" projection would save nothing measurable and would
/// buy a second thing to keep in step with the concept. The moment a field
/// arrives that a list should not carry -- a long note, an attachment -- that
/// is the day to split it, and not before.
@row
shape account clientAccountFull {
  row.id
  ownerUserId
  name
  domain
  domains
  defaultDomain
  defaultSenderIdentityId
  primaryContactName
  primaryContactEmail
  notes
  status
  domainToken
  domainStatus
  domainFailureReason
  domainFailureDetail
  domainLastCheckedAt
  domainVerifiedAt
  joinOnDomain
  memqlDomain
  memqlReservedAt
  memqlReservationReason
  configuredAt
  row.createdAt
}

/// Id-only projection for the boot group backfill. The sweep needs nothing but
/// the id -- it hands each one to groupEnsureForAccount, which reads the row
/// it needs for itself.
@row
shape account accountIdRef {
  row.id
}

/// The slice of an account the domain walk reads: the name to check, the token
/// to check it with, and the reservation fields it stamps on success.
@row
shape account accountDomainWalk {
  row.id
  domain
  domainToken
  domainStatus
  memqlDomain
  memqlReservedAt
}
